WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:11.160
Whether you're shopping for goods

00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:13.320
or wanting a taste of local flavor,

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:15.540
street markets offer a special look inside

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:17.570
of the culture of a community.

00:00:17.570 --> 00:00:20.010
From live seafood on your plate in Tokyo

00:00:20.010 --> 00:00:22.210
to ancient rituals in La Paz,

00:00:22.210 --> 00:00:25.010
you'll find something
different everywhere you go.

00:00:25.010 --> 00:00:27.760
Here is what street markets
look like around the world.

00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:39.970
The Queen Victoria Market is
the largest open-air market

00:00:39.970 --> 00:00:41.640
in the southern hemisphere.

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:44.760
Often referred to as
Vic Market or Queen Vic,

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:46.850
the market has been serving
the city of Melbourne

00:00:46.850 --> 00:00:48.790
since 1878.

00:00:48.790 --> 00:00:51.430
The market even hosts
an ultimate foodie tour

00:00:51.430 --> 00:00:53.470
where visitors can learn
the history of the market

00:00:53.470 --> 00:00:56.163
and indulge in the best
foods it has to offer.

00:01:02.630 --> 00:01:04.222
Once called Tsukiji Market,

00:01:04.222 --> 00:01:06.600
the newly relocated Toyosu Market

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:10.450
is a massive wholesale seafood market.

00:01:10.450 --> 00:01:12.660
It is most known for the tuna auction,

00:01:12.660 --> 00:01:15.990
which occurs between 5:30 and 6:30 a.m.

00:01:15.990 --> 00:01:19.240
Visitors can watch the auction
from an observation deck.

00:01:19.240 --> 00:01:22.210
The market also features
fresh produce for purchase

00:01:22.210 --> 00:01:24.713
and restaurants from the
original Tsukiji Market.

00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:35.210
The Jagalchi Market sells
a wide variety of seafood.

00:01:35.210 --> 00:01:38.160
Grab a bucket to pick out
your food on the ground floor.

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:41.290
Take your seafood to go or
have it prepared into a meal

00:01:41.290 --> 00:01:43.640
at one of the restaurants
on the second floor.

00:01:43.640 --> 00:01:46.353
The market sells both
dried and live seafood.

00:01:52.780 --> 00:01:54.560
Night markets have always been prevalent

00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:56.980
in Asian nightlife culture
dating all the way back to

00:01:56.980 --> 00:01:58.470
the Tang dynasty.

00:01:58.470 --> 00:01:59.770
When the sun goes down,

00:01:59.770 --> 00:02:01.730
Temple Street Night Market comes alive

00:02:01.730 --> 00:02:04.000
with bustling visitors and food stands

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:06.230
cooking up decadent street food.

00:02:06.230 --> 00:02:08.530
Take your pick from
buckets of fresh seafood

00:02:08.530 --> 00:02:11.053
or wander through the
various market stalls.

00:02:21.270 --> 00:02:24.380
Though it sits remotely in
the westernmost part of China,

00:02:24.380 --> 00:02:27.860
Kashgar Bazaar is often packed
with around 100,000 visitors

00:02:27.860 --> 00:02:28.880
each Sunday.

00:02:28.880 --> 00:02:30.520
Beyond the souvenirs and trinkets,

00:02:30.520 --> 00:02:32.750
you can find stunning silks and rugs,

00:02:32.750 --> 00:02:36.450
spices and nuts, and plenty
of street eats to bite into.

00:02:36.450 --> 00:02:38.670
A common saying in the area
is that you can purchase

00:02:38.670 --> 00:02:41.523
anything at Kashgar Bazaar
except chicken's milk.

00:02:51.950 --> 00:02:53.170
This market in Thailand

00:02:53.170 --> 00:02:56.300
is one of the most famous
floating markets in the world.

00:02:56.300 --> 00:02:58.473
Located about 60 miles outside of Bangkok,

00:02:58.473 --> 00:03:01.760
Damnoen Saduak features longtail boats

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:03.420
that drift along the market.

00:03:03.420 --> 00:03:05.480
Visitors can purchase fresh produce,

00:03:05.480 --> 00:03:07.863
souvenirs, and an array of snacks.

00:03:15.820 --> 00:03:17.230
The Mallik Ghat Flower Market

00:03:17.230 --> 00:03:19.860
is the one of the biggest
flower markets in Asia.

00:03:19.860 --> 00:03:21.880
Flowers could sell out as early as noon,

00:03:21.880 --> 00:03:24.610
so vendors start their days at 4 a.m.

00:03:24.610 --> 00:03:27.203
Blocks of ice are used to
keep the flowers fresh.

00:03:28.670 --> 00:03:30.850
The market boasts an
array of colorful flowers

00:03:30.850 --> 00:03:33.690
including roses, jasmine, and marigolds,

00:03:33.690 --> 00:03:36.600
which are all used to
make malas, or garland.

00:03:36.600 --> 00:03:39.270
Malas are commonly used
for religious rituals,

00:03:39.270 --> 00:03:43.113
ceremonies, and as decoration
for houses, roads, and cities.

00:03:49.600 --> 00:03:53.300
Discover thousands of spices
at the Dubai Spice Souk.

00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:56.150
Shoppers can haggle for herbs,
dried fruits and flowers,

00:03:56.150 --> 00:03:57.723
and even natural deodorant.

00:04:09.310 --> 00:04:11.710
Grand Bazaar is one of
the biggest and oldest

00:04:11.710 --> 00:04:13.100
covered markets in the world,

00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:15.570
dating back to the 15th century.

00:04:15.570 --> 00:04:17.375
Once a staple of the Ottoman Empire,

00:04:17.375 --> 00:04:20.700
the market today houses over 4,000 shops.

00:04:20.700 --> 00:04:22.340
Wander through the maze of hallways

00:04:22.340 --> 00:04:25.000
where decadent Turkish
treats, colorful textiles,

00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:27.360
and mosaic lamps light up the halls.

00:04:27.360 --> 00:04:30.123
Authentic handmade Turkish
rugs are a great souvenir.

00:04:37.150 --> 00:04:40.150
The Izmailovsky Market is a
hidden treasure tucked inside

00:04:40.150 --> 00:04:41.700
the Izmailovo Kremlin.

00:04:41.700 --> 00:04:44.850
The market is the ultimate stop
for authentic Russian treats

00:04:44.850 --> 00:04:47.883
and souvenirs like the
famous Matryoshka doll.

00:04:53.300 --> 00:04:56.720
Christmas markets are a European
staple during the holidays.

00:04:56.720 --> 00:04:58.260
Prague hosts its Christmas markets

00:04:58.260 --> 00:05:00.940
from the end of November
to the beginning of January

00:05:00.940 --> 00:05:03.270
with the main markets
held in Old Town Square

00:05:03.270 --> 00:05:04.770
and Wenceslas Square.

00:05:04.770 --> 00:05:07.850
The market is lined with food
stalls offering small bites

00:05:07.850 --> 00:05:11.300
like roasted chestnuts, chips
on a stick, and chimney cake

00:05:11.300 --> 00:05:12.970
known as trdelník.

00:05:12.970 --> 00:05:16.160
Visitors can also warm up
with a cup of mulled wine

00:05:16.160 --> 00:05:18.753
and shop handmade trinkets and souvenirs.

00:05:26.360 --> 00:05:28.440
Venetians rely on the Rialto Market

00:05:28.440 --> 00:05:31.520
for their fruits, vegetables,
and other goods each day.

00:05:31.520 --> 00:05:33.760
For seafood lovers, the Pescaria offers up

00:05:33.760 --> 00:05:35.910
some of the freshest
sea critters in Venice,

00:05:35.910 --> 00:05:38.693
many of which are purchased
by restaurants in the area.

00:05:50.720 --> 00:05:53.370
What was once a pig market in 1470

00:05:53.370 --> 00:05:55.890
is now a thriving corner of Barcelona

00:05:55.890 --> 00:05:57.943
known as Mercado de la Boqueria.

00:05:58.900 --> 00:06:00.830
Sometimes referred to as
the heart of the city,

00:06:00.830 --> 00:06:02.510
the market features an array

00:06:02.510 --> 00:06:05.363
of quality meats, cheeses,
produce, and more.

00:06:15.110 --> 00:06:16.990
By day, you can find an array of goods

00:06:16.990 --> 00:06:19.740
and even snake charmers at Jemaa el-Fnaa.

00:06:19.740 --> 00:06:22.040
By night, the square
lights up with food stands

00:06:22.040 --> 00:06:24.093
serving authentic Moroccan cuisine.

00:06:35.281 --> 00:06:38.550
Ver-o-peso offers fruits,
vegetables, and medicinal herbs

00:06:38.550 --> 00:06:40.240
from the rainforest.

00:06:40.240 --> 00:06:42.200
It also hosts the Açaí Fair

00:06:42.200 --> 00:06:45.673
where açaí is sold and
consumed in its natural form.

00:06:53.190 --> 00:06:56.190
You can find potions,
spells, and medicinal goods

00:06:56.190 --> 00:06:57.750
at this Bolivian market.

00:06:57.750 --> 00:06:59.230
The Witches' Market sells goods

00:06:59.230 --> 00:07:02.160
based on traditional
medicines and rituals.

00:07:02.160 --> 00:07:05.770
The market's most notable
item is a dried llama fetus,

00:07:05.770 --> 00:07:08.170
which is said to bring
good luck and protection.

00:07:17.380 --> 00:07:19.290
You'll find vendors
selling their homegrown

00:07:19.290 --> 00:07:22.450
and handcrafted goods in the
bustling Castries Market.

00:07:22.450 --> 00:07:24.700
The market was originally built in 1891

00:07:24.700 --> 00:07:26.900
to improve the town and has since become

00:07:26.900 --> 00:07:29.690
the largest open-air market in the area.

00:07:29.690 --> 00:07:30.950
Shop the various stalls

00:07:30.950 --> 00:07:33.233
or soak up the vibrant Castries scene.

00:07:41.420 --> 00:07:45.290
Chichicastenango is one of
Guatemala's most vibrant markets.

00:07:45.290 --> 00:07:47.930
Vendors sell colorful
textiles, fresh produce,

00:07:47.930 --> 00:07:51.810
and an abundance of flowers
sold on the steps of the church.

00:07:51.810 --> 00:07:55.070
Also called Chichi, the market
is only open on Thursdays

00:07:55.070 --> 00:07:56.173
and Saturdays.

00:08:05.350 --> 00:08:08.060
Cental de Abasto is one of
the largest wholesale markets

00:08:08.060 --> 00:08:11.010
in the world with over
2,000 businesses covering

00:08:11.010 --> 00:08:13.198
over 800 acres.

00:08:13.198 --> 00:08:14.889
Thirty thousand tons of merchandise

00:08:14.889 --> 00:08:16.880
go through the market each day.

00:08:16.880 --> 00:08:19.560
The market is lined with
colorful fruits and vegetables,

00:08:19.560 --> 00:08:22.350
many of which make their way
into hundreds of restaurants

00:08:22.350 --> 00:08:24.243
and food stands in the city each day.

00:08:31.820 --> 00:08:35.380
Pike Place Market is a staple
in the Pacific Northwest.

00:08:35.380 --> 00:08:39.130
The market has been serving
the community since 1907.

00:08:39.130 --> 00:08:42.570
Colorful produce, handmade
pasta, and plenty of fish

00:08:42.570 --> 00:08:45.610
sold by local fishmongers
are available each day.

00:08:45.610 --> 00:08:48.720
Pike Place Fish Market is
best known for its tradition

00:08:48.720 --> 00:08:51.720
of tossing customers' orders
across the shopping area.

00:08:51.720 --> 00:08:53.600
Watch as they toss the fish around,

00:08:53.600 --> 00:08:55.113
or try catching your own.

00:09:01.410 --> 00:09:04.020
New York City is a melting
pot of food innovation

00:09:04.020 --> 00:09:06.180
influenced by multiple cultures.

00:09:06.180 --> 00:09:09.310
All over the city, glossy food
halls with dozens of options

00:09:09.310 --> 00:09:11.783
are popping up, like
the Canal Street Market.

00:09:13.300 --> 00:09:16.510
Some options include
so-called food mashups

00:09:16.510 --> 00:09:17.963
like sushi burritos.

